 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "`IsTarskiSeed.mod` at Tarski.lean:64 has no use anywhere (grep for `IsTarskiSeed.` returns only `exists_identity`, `mul_derivative`, `sum_sign_eq_zero`, `sturmSeq`); the seed hypothesis shape appears at Tarski.lean:225,243 and Infinity.lean:112,134,156; Mathlib's `Algebra/Polynomial/Sturm/Sequence.lean` contains no `tail` lemma (grep `tail` \u2192 no matches), so nothing downstream supplies it.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Polynomial/Sturm/Tarski.lean",
   "fix": "Expose the bridge as a lemma, e.g. `theorem head?_tail_sturmSeq (hp : p \u2260 0) : (sturmSeq p q).tail.head?.getD 0 = q` (holds for `q = 0` too, since `sturmSeq p 0 = [p]`), prove `IsTarskiSeed.sturmSeq` from it plus `mul_derivative`, and add the reduced-seed specialization `IsTarskiSeed p f ((sturmSeq p ((f * p.derivative) % p)).tail.head?.getD 0)`; if reduced seeds are out of scope, delete `IsTarskiSeed.mod` instead of leaving it unusable.",
   "issue": "`IsTarskiSeed.mod` is public but unreachable from any exposed chain: every general theorem (`sum_sign`, `sum_sign_of_squarefree`, `sum_sign_Ioi/Iio/univ`) demands `IsTarskiSeed p f (cs.head?.getD 0)`, and the fact that identifies that seed for Mathlib's sequence is inlined in `IsTarskiSeed.sturmSeq` (lines 97-104) rather than stated. A consumer using the reduced query `(f * p.derivative) % p` \u2014 the variant the PR description advertises \u2014 must re-derive the `sturmSeq_cons` / `head?_sturmSeq` / zero-remainder case split by hand, so the abstract seed API can in practice only be instantiated at the unreduced `f * p'` query.",
   "line": "64"
  }
 ],
